  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fca Us obligated $506M in FY2026 to date, across 11,695 awards with an average award size of $43.3K. Obligations are up 99.1% year over year. Annual obligations show a volatile pattern: FY21 totaled $267M, FY22 totaled $16.1M, FY23 totaled $356M, FY24 totaled $330M, FY25 totaled $254M, and FY26 to date totaled $506M. Award activity is high given the award count, while the average award size indicates a mix of many smaller awards and some larger awards. The note clarifies that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights recent scale and volatility in obligations and shows that FY26 year-to-date obligations exceed prior full fiscal-year totals for several years listed. Readers should treat FY26 as a partial year total when comparing across years.",
